      <description>The Centre for Natural Resource Governance (CNRG) has raised serious allegations that some Zimbabwean journalists were offered money to undermine community testimony during a press conference addressing grave exhumations linked to lithium mining in Buhera, in a development that has reignited debate over media ethics, corporate influence and the treatment of rural communities in mining areas.</description>
